-- title:
--   Nilpotent tuples lie in ker[p^v] for large v
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $d$, and let $\Phi_0$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathbb{Z}/p$: a $d$-tuple of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \sqcup \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ whose constant coefficients vanish, whose linear coefficients in each of the two blocks of variables are $\delta_{ij}$, and which is associative in the usual substitution sense; assume moreover that $\Phi_0$ is commutative, i.e. interchanging the two blocks of variables leaves each component unchanged. Let $(G^c_v)_{v \in \mathbb{N}}$ be commutative $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebras, and for each $v$ let $\kappa_v : (\mathbb{Z}/p)[[X_1,\dots,X_d]] \to G^c_v$ be a surjective $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra homomorphism whose kernel is the ideal generated by the $d$ components of $\Phi_0.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,(p^v)$, where $\mathrm{nthSeries}$ is defined recursively by $\mathrm{nthSeries}\,0 = 0$ and $\mathrm{nthSeries}\,(n+1)_i = \Phi_0{}_i(\mathrm{nthSeries}\,n, X)$, so that it is the $n$-fold multiplication series $[n]_{\Phi_0}$. Let $S$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra and $x : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to S$ a tuple all of whose entries are nilpotent. Then there exist a level $v$ and a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra homomorphism $f : G^c_v \to S$ with $f(\kappa_v(X_i)) = x_i$ for every $i$.
--
--   In geometric terms: the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebras $G^c_v$ present the kernels $\ker[p^v]$ of multiplication by $p^v$ on $\Phi_0$, and the assertion is that every tuple of nilpotent elements of an $\mathbb{F}_p$-algebra $S$ is the coordinate vector of an $S$-valued point of $\ker[p^v]_{\Phi_0}$ once $v$ is large enough, the point being that over $\mathbb{F}_p$ the order of $[p^v]_{\Phi_0}$ grows with $v$. It supplies test points on the special fibre of a $p$-divisible group and is used in the construction of the formal group and cocycle attached to a Honda system with split coordinates.
-- source:
